WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.600
Bosnia is home to three main ethnic

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.079
groups. The Bosniaks, who are mostly

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.320
Muslim, the Serbs who are mostly orthodox

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.479
Christian and the Croats—they're mostly

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.880
Catholic. And don't get confused with

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:10.880
Serbians or Croatians, which is what

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.960
people from Serbia and Croatia are

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.040
called, although they share history,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.080
tradition and religion with the Serbs

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.400
and Croats. Now, Bosnia's ethnic divisions

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.600
were a big part of the war that happened

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.600
in the 1990s. After Yugoslavia broke up,

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.439
there was a power vacuum and all those

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.119
ethnic groups started fighting each

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:32.320
other for territory.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:34.400
In 1992, the UN recognised Bosnia and

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.640
Herzegovina's independence, and that

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.280
didn't go down well with Serbs.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.159
Various Serb forces attacked, and that

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:44.079
was the start of the Bosnian war.

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.960
Fighting went on for three-and-a-half

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:47.439
years.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.200
Atrocities were committed by all sides.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.520
Roughly 100,000 people were

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.560
killed, about 80% were

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.040
Bosniaks. In the town of Srebrenica,

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.399
Serb forces killed more than 8,000

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:03.759
Bosnian Muslims—men and boys. A UN

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:06.799
tribunal later called it a genocide.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:09.119
The war ended in 1995, with the Dayton

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:12.160
Peace Agreement, a deal brokered by the

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:14.400
US. Europe and Russia were also involved.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.800
It included a new constitution for

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.280
Bosnia that tried to balance political

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.000
power between the Bosniaks, Serbs and

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.560
Croats. But in many ways, that

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.200
constitution only reinforced those

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.280
ethnic divisions. 

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.239
So keep that

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.319
in mind while we tell you what the

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:50.560
system looks like. There's the state

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:52.800
level that deals with the whole country,

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.640
but instead of one president at the top, 

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.440
they have what's called a tripartite

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.440
presidency. It means three people share

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.319
the presidency, and it's always one

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:04.159
Bosniak, one Croat and one Serb. There's

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:06.000
also a prime minister and a parliament

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:08.080
at the state level. And this is where

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.400
things like foreign policy and the army

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.720
are dealt with. At the next level down,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.640
you've got two self-governing entities.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.200
There's Republika Srpska and the

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.040
Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina. And

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.640
don't confuse the federation with the

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.239
name of the country.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.560
And there are more layers of government

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:26.319
below those, but there's another layer we

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.280
need to talk about. And that's back at

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:31.120
the top—the high representative. 

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:46.239
The high

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.159
representative is never a Bosnian.

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:50.400
They're usually from the EU. The current

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:52.000
one's German. So, in some ways, you can

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.400
think of Bosnia as a kind of

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.319
protectorate. It really depends on the

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.360
international community, especially the

00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:01.519
US and EU, to keep the peace. The whole

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.000
system is completely rooted in the

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:06.400
Dayton agreement. But right now, that

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.879
system is looking a bit shaky.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.840
A lot of that has to do with this man,

00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:14.000
Milorad Dodik. He's the Serb member of

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:17.759
the tripartite presidency. 

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.330
And that rhetoric has

00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:33.280
risen in the last few months.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.759
Dodik threatened to pull out Republika

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:40.000
Srpska from the main state-level

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:42.320
institutions—the judiciary, the tax

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.040
authority and the army—and set up

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.759
separate Serb ones. 

00:04:55.199 --> 00:04:59.759
Serb politicians have also

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.320
been refusing to participate in many

00:04:59.759 --> 00:05:04.400
state-level institutions. It's paralysing

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.360
the system and nothing's really getting

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.000
done.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.759
And then in Republika Srpska they went

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.919
ahead with celebrations to mark what

00:05:09.759 --> 00:05:16.840
they call their National Day, which

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:16.840
Bosnia's top court has ruled illegal.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.680
Now, there are a couple reasons why

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.840
things have heated up so much lately.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.000
Last July, the high representative at the

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.240
time—remember that's the top foreign

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.639
official we talked about earlier—he

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.720
brought in a new law to make genocide

00:05:52.639 --> 00:05:56.319
denial a crime.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.400
It's something that Bosniaks, in

00:05:56.319 --> 00:05:59.440
particular, have been calling for for a

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.440
while.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:03.840
The law doesn't single out any ethnic

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.400
group, but many Serbs feel the law

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.880
unfairly targets them, and Dodik and his

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.199
allies have pushed this idea, too. 

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:41.520
There's another big

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:44.080
thing going on that Dodik is unhappy

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:46.240
about. It's a long-running dispute over

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:49.039
public agricultural land within

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.840
Republika Srpska. Dodik insists it

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:54.319
belongs to Republika Srpska, but Bosnia's

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:56.560
Constitutional Court declared it belongs

00:06:54.319 --> 00:06:59.280
to the state. So Dodik wants that

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:01.680
decision overturned, and he's using it as

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.080
a bargaining chip. 

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.919
Now there's

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:12.720
another dimension to all of this:

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:15.039
elections, which are in October. It means

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.599
a lot of politicians are riled up,

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:18.800
including Dodik. 

00:07:46.479 --> 00:07:50.720
So that paints the

00:07:48.319 --> 00:07:53.520
picture of what's going on inside Bosnia.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.680
But what about the role of the US, the EU

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.599
and NATO in all of this?

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.479
They're the guarantors of the Dayton

00:07:57.599 --> 00:08:00.960
agreement.

00:07:58.479 --> 00:08:02.639
The US imposed new sanctions on Dodik

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.599
for what they called "significant

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:07.919
corruption and destabilising activities".

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:10.560
And the EU has a small peacekeeping

00:08:07.919 --> 00:08:11.599
force in Bosnia, currently around 600

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.599
soldiers.

00:08:11.599 --> 00:08:16.160
But some people think that's just not

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:18.240
nearly enough, and is one of the reasons

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.960
things have gone this far. 

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.320
The big shadow over this whole

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:02.640
crisis is the fear that it could

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.560
escalate into another conflict. And

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.880
Bosnians are all too familiar with the

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.040
worst-case scenario. So even though some

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.279
people say Dodik isn't serious about

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.920
following through with secession,

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:14.959
just by raising it he also raises the

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.760
stakes.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.519
If you found that useful, check out our

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.519
recent explainer on what's happening in

00:09:59.519 --> 00:10:03.760
Ukraine. And if you have other ideas for

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:08.600
news stories you want explained, let us

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:08.600
know in the comments. See you next week.

